Security Audit Report
CRITICAL (Fix immediately)
1. Unauthenticated debug endpoint — routes/admin.php:27-40
A public route /admin/debug/auth-status dumps full session data, user objects, and guard info to anyone — no auth required. Remove it.

2. Mass assignment on ~45 models — app/Models/*.php
Models including User, Deposit, Withdrawal, Transaction, Order etc. have no $fillable or $guarded. Any create() or update($request->all()) call can overwrite sensitive columns like balance, is_admin, status.

3. Unprotected cron/test routes — routes/web.php:6-30
Routes like /cron, /stageOne, /reconAll/{stage}, /clear, and /test are publicly accessible with no auth middleware. /clear runs optimize:clear. The cron routes can trigger financial logic.

4. XSS in JSON responses — SiteController.php:319-340
User data is interpolated raw into HTML strings returned as JSON:


return response()->json(['msg' => "<input value='$user->id' ...>"]);
A crafted username with "><script> payload executes in other users' browsers.

5. IDOR in activateAccount() — ManageUsersController.php:235-285
The route parameter $id is ignored; the function reads $request->user_id directly. Any authenticated admin (or CSRF-forced request) can activate any arbitrary user account and trigger a 900-balance bonus to their referrer.

HIGH
6. SMS gateway credentials in URLs — app/Notify/SmsGateway.php:46-79
Passwords and API keys for Infobip, SMSBroadcast, and Clickatell are passed as GET query parameters — they end up in server access logs, proxy logs, and referrer headers in plaintext.

7. orderByRaw() without binding — AdminSavingsController.php:18
Pattern is safe today but no binding is used. If user input ever flows into an orderByRaw() call, it's direct SQL injection.

MEDIUM
8. No permission checks on deposit approve/reject — DepositController.php
Any admin-guard user can approve or reject deposits regardless of their role. $request->message is stored raw as admin feedback with no sanitization.

9. Disabled old-password verification — ManageUsersController.php:40-43
The old-password check is commented out. Any admin can reset any user's password silently.

10. Null pointer risk — ManageUsersController.php:245
User::find() can return null; the next line calls ->profile_complete = 1 without a null check. Use findOrFail().

11. Exception suppression with @ — SmsGateway.php:50, 55, 78
@file_get_contents(...) silently swallows all errors — SMS delivery failures produce no logs and no errors.

